zl1: what the third heat cause is worth in temperature -- the three-window A/B/C run, 2026-09-25
================================================================================================

ONE BOOT, read before and after and unchanged: boot_id 2fbf9f8e-deea-4955-ad0c-6bddf0fb14f5.
Nothing was flashed, no partition was written, no service was started or stopped, and no reboot was
taken. The run writes ONE file twice -- /sys/module/lpm_levels/parameters/sleep_disabled, `1` for
window B and `0` again for window C -- and puts it back to the INSTALLED state (0/N) on every exit
path; the device's own 06-lpm-fix unit also re-applies 0 on every boot, so this cannot outlive one.

The device was identified by SERIAL (33e80afe-v63-usbd-disabled-rndis on 3-3), not by USB id: an
unrelated device with a Google vendor id shares this bus.

WHY THREE WINDOWS: this phone's idle temperature drifts on its own -- two read-only windows an hour
apart read the hottest tsens zone at 45.6 C and then 50.9 C with nothing changed in between. So A
(the ladder allowed, as installed) is followed by B (the ladder blocked) and then by C, which is A's
state again. C is the CONTROL: if the warming that appears in B is still there in C, the run says
so instead of reporting the difference as the ladder's price.


